          </h4>
          <p style="color: #1e3a8a; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
            The original four Aldabra giant tortoises were a gift from the British Governor of the Seychelles to the Sultan of Zanzibar in 1919. Over a century later, dedicated conservation rangers safeguard their thriving descendants. Each tortoise has their age painted in white on their shell. Visitors are invited to gently stroke their necks (which they stretch out appreciatively!) and feed them fresh leafy cabbage provided by rangers.
          </p>
